    RefIds:
    - rid: 1000
      type: {class: BtRoot, ns: CGD.BehaviorTrees, asm: CGD.Runtime}
      data:
        _guid: ee7696869a6d413ead9ebb2c4d141e61
        _position: {x: 0, y: 0}
        _comment: 'TECH siege (sentinel): not a tank but the squad''s siege engine, a slow, heavily plated machine that holds its own post well behind the other Tech, 12 m behind the ally nearest the threat in high cover, and makes cover useless to the enemy. When a target ducks behind cover or into a bush it shells the spot with a Mortar Shell every 5 s (no line of sight needed), pours suppressing fire into it between shells and watches it for the target breaking cover; a target in the open gets a Missile Salvo (Signature) to drive it back into hiding where the mortar finds it. When a squadmate is worn down and falling back it covers the retreat: a Smoke Mortar onto the enemy so it loses sight of the squad, then it leaves its post and pushes in through the smoke at its best pace for up to 15 s, burning and shoving back anything within 7 m with its Flamethrower (every 25 s at most). Otherwise it covers the field from its post with suppressing fire. It grenades anything within 12 m, Fortifies under fire (Boost) and bashes what reaches it (Special). Kit: Signature (Missile Salvo), Boost (Fortify), Special (Weapon Bash), Grenade (Tech Grenade); the Mortar Shell, Smoke Mortar and Flamethrower are set on the tree.'
        _children:
        - 48af69ace776475abcd200328cfeb94c
